d-df52-57c7-8623-19ca9f0bd498" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350321 1145 "The position function of a particle moving in a circular path of radius $a$ in the $xy$-plane with a constant angular velocity $\\omega $ is given by\n\n$$\nr(t)=a(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t\\,j),\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that the circle is centered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(a,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=2$ and $\\omega =1\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity and acceleration vectors by differentiating. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ a(t) & =(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the acceleration vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,i-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,i-\\frac{2}{2}\\,j \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\,i-\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350323 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350324 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350325 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350326 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350327 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1041 "selection" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350323 13194139535458 true] [17592186350322 1110 #uuid "e477cef2-d4df-5e9d-aa37-503abefe3a08" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350323 1034 "-\\sq