ered at $O,$ and the particle is at the position $(a,0)$ when $t=0.$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=4$ and $\\omega =3\\text{ rad/s},$ so we get that the position function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe find the velocity and acceleration vectors by differentiating. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =(4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j))^{′} \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+12\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j \\\\ a(t) & =(-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,i+12\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,j)^{′} \\\\  & =-36\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,i-36\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the acceleration vector at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-36\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,i-36\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,j \\\\  & =-36\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\,i-36\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\,j \\\\  & =36\\,i\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350330 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350331 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350332 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350333 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1000 #edb/ref 17592186350334 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1041 "selection" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1104 #edb/ref 17592186350334 13194139535458 true] [17592186350329 1110 #uuid "c3b3ce91-a44a-5424-ab02-c446ccbd8457" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350330 1034 "-12\\,i-12\\,j" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350330 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535458 true] [17592186350330 1111 #uuid "8207b716-5073-567a-8b5a-f7e65fa4ddbe" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350331 1034 "36\\,j" 13194139535458 true] [17592186350331 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535458 true] [175921863